> when I try to run the inspect() function on the model, I get this error:  Error in lavListInspect(object = object, what = what, add.labels = TRUE,  : object 'fit' not found.
> It will run inspect fine if I only put the model, but as soon as I try to get fit-indices or anything else, I get that error. This is not the case when I run inspect() with a non-imputed model.

That is because inspect() is only a method for a lavaan-class or lavaanList-class object.  runMI() returns a lavaan.mi-class object, which inherits from the lavaanList-class (as you can see in the error message, the inspect() method notices this and tries to run the lavListInspect() function).  So, if you want to use inspect() on a lavaan.mi object, see the ?lavListInspect help page for information that it would be possible to request.

For other types of other information, please read the class?lavaan.mi help page for a description of the available methods.  If you are looking for for fit indices, for example, you can use the anova() method.

fit.mi <- runMI(...)
anova(fit.mi, indices = "all")

Also see the helpful examples and notes on the ?runMI help page, where I did my best to demonstrate the new functionality.

Terrence D. Jorgensen
Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics
Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam
