I have been working in a dataset comprised of cognitive and brain volumetric data. The aim is to compare two groups, cases and controls for a certain condition. The model include e latent variable in a MIMIC design.

The design is similar to previous experiments that worked out fine, but in this particular case I do not get scalar invariance btw groups. The only thing that is different from previous experiments using other datasets is that now the cognitive data is a z-scored sum of item scores, previously I used data from principal component analysis.

How can I diagnose what indicators are involved in this?

Here is a MWE with anonymized data:
install.packages("RCurl")
library(RCurl)

test<- read.csv(text = getURL("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lf-araujo/sempsychiatry/master/MWE.csv"))

semModelMIMIC <- '
g =~ A+B+C+ D
g ~ E
+   F
+   G
+   H
+ I
+ J
+K
+L
'

fitInter <- sem(semModelMIMIC, data = test,  estimator = "MLM")
fitmeasures(fitInter, c("df", "rmsea", "cfi", "aic", "chisq", "pvalue"))

